®\Å!\ÊJuUYœJ[/\ëS}\n\Ó\ÖüQ\äƒM½¡\ÙoÁ\Ëd\ëS\à7™\é‘6\å†úH\ÙBüö\ÅyŸ\Ý\Å6ý>Æ’h\Ú\Ñ>_ý\åö\Õñ\ì¶Å²zh²}N«bk%ºŸ%l<¢t\Õ\ê\ßož\Þzí¢\æ\0\0\0',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'In 2024, the Honda NSX celebrates 35 years since its debut, marking a milestone for one of the most revolutionary Japanese supercars. Developed in the 1980s, the NSX was Hondaâ€™s answer to Ferrari and Porsche, bringing cutting-edge technology, lightweight construction, and race-inspired engineering to the streets.\nThe development of the NSX began in 1985 under the codename NS-X (New Sportscar eXperimental). It was designed with a mid-engine layout, an all-aluminum monocoque chassis, and Formula 1-inspired innovations, setting a new standard for performance and reliability in the supercar world.\n\nThe first-generation NSX featured a 3.0L V6 engine with VTEC, producing 270 hp and accelerating from 0-100 km/h in 5.9 seconds. In 1997, the engine was upgraded to a 3.2L V6 with 290 hp, improving performance further. Production of the first-generation NSX ended in 2005, and in 2016, Honda introduced the second-generation NSX with a hybrid powertrain producing 573 hp.',3,'2025-01-19 18:16:37','2025-01-19 18:16:37');
